    "updated_at": "2017-05-17T17:09:51Z",
    "body": "@annevk With the current spec text, you cannot match namespace-less attributes with a name in uppercase in HTML elements in HTML documents (which are also never produced by the parser). With my proposed change, that would be the case regardless of namespace. But still only on HTML elements in HTML documents.\r\n\r\nI don’t understand your point about sharing stylesheets. The \"in HTML documents\" bit is about the element being matched, not about the stylesheet.",
